From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 16:42:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS ARM64EC: add JIT-pool alias awareness to FEX range
 trackers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When ARM64EC PE images are copied into the iOS JIT pool (so they can
actually be marked RX — iOS rejects mprotect(RX) on file-backed mmaps),
the copy lives at a different address than the original PE load address.
FEX's InvalidationTracker and ImageTracker only know the original PE
address ranges, so any query for a JIT-alias address (e.g.
0x11fc225fe = sechost-copy's offset 0x1e5fe) returns "not executable"
→ FEX emits NoExecOp → the translation traps when executed.

This commit adds the FEX-side infrastructure to handle this:

1. New export BTCpu64IosAddAliasMapping(PeBase, JitBase, Size) — added
   to the def file and BTInterface so Wine ntdll can bind and call it.
   Stores entries in a static table (256 entries × 32B = 8KB; struct
   padded to 32B so the array stride is a power of 2, keeping ADRP+LDR
   relocations alignment-clean).

2. IosJitTranslate / IosJitReverseTranslate helpers — forward/reverse
   alias-to-PE coordinate translation against the table.

3. ECSyscallHandler overrides for QueryGuestExecutableRange and
   LookupExecutableFileSection now do: query tracker; if miss, reverse-
   translate alias→PE, query again, forward-translate result back to
   alias coords. Wrapped in #ifdef FEX_IOS_HOST.

The table + accessors live in IosJitAlias.cpp rather than Module.cpp —
accessing the static array directly from class-method overrides in
Module.cpp triggered "misaligned ldr/str offset" link errors, almost
certainly an ADRP+LDR page-offset issue specific to ARM64EC hybrid
emit in class-method contexts. Putting the data + accessors in their
own TU and accessing them via plain extern "C" function calls is clean.

NOTE: the table is not yet populated by Wine ntdll-unix. Without the
Wine PE→unix bridge to push the iOS JIT mappings through
BTCpu64IosAddAliasMapping, this code is dormant — it falls through to
the existing tracker behavior. That bridge is the next work item.

